From: George Wilkins <george@hellas.ai>
Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: thermal: cv1800: bridge thermal zone into hwmon

Stacks on top of Haylen Chu's cv1800-thermal driver (our 0006)
to register the thermal zone with the kernel's hwmon interface,
so /sys/class/hwmon/hwmonN/temp1_input shows up alongside the
canonical /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp. Lets the same
userspace tooling (lm-sensors, glances, prometheus-node-exporter,
...) that already finds the iio-hwmon-bridged SAR-ADC voltages
also pick up the SoC die temperature without bespoke parsing of
/sys/class/thermal.

Local addition to the LKML v5 series; if/when that lands in
mainline this patch can be folded into the upstream driver
(qcom/tsens.c and several other in-tree thermal drivers do the
same call already).

Signed-off-by: George Wilkins <george@hellas.ai>
---
--- a/drivers/thermal/cv1800_thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/cv1800_thermal.c
@@ -14,6 +14,8 @@
 #include <linux/thermal.h>
 #include <linux/units.h>
 
+#include "thermal_hwmon.h"
+
 #define TEMPSEN_VERSION					0x0
 #define TEMPSEN_CTRL					0x4
 #define  TEMPSEN_CTRL_EN				BIT(0)
@@ -244,6 +246,8 @@
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret, "failed to request irq\n");
 
+	devm_thermal_add_hwmon_sysfs(&pdev->dev, tdev);
+
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, ctz);
 
 	return 0;
